# Read by every bash script that Steam starts (BASH_ENV, set in nx-steam-arm64); acts only on
# the one that starts Steam's embedded browser (steamwebhelper.sh, Valve's file - not edited, a
# client update would undo that).
# The browser draws Steam's windows with the GPU. In the GPU driver's tiled mode its drawing
# reaches a few rows past the end of the window's image whenever a window is resized or
# redrawn (kernel log: "GPU PAGE FAULT ... name=steamwebhelper ... FAULTING BLOCK: CCU", address
# just behind a mapped buffer; thousands per session) - the windows then went black for a
# moment. Drawing straight into the image ("sysmem" mode) does not do that: 0 faults over the
# same resize test that gave 665. Games do not get this setting.
case "$0" in
*steamwebhelper.sh) export TU_DEBUG=sysmem ;;
esac
